## 2. Fluxo de Erro: Timeout no Complete

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Backend API
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant DB as Database
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Queue
    
    FE->>+API: POST /media/complete
    API->>+S3: CompleteMultipartUpload
    
    Note over S3: S3 demora >30s<br/>(consolidando 40 chunks)
    
    S3-->>API: ⏳ Timeout (30s)
    
    API->>API: Catch Timeout Exception
    
    API->>+DB: UPDATE media_files<br/>SET status='completing'<br/>(estado intermediário)
    DB-->>-API: OK
    
    API->>+DLQ: Enqueue RetryCompleteJob<br/>{uploadId, mediaFileId, retryCount=1}
    DLQ-->>-API: OK (job enfileirado)
    
    API-->>-FE: 202 Accepted {<br/>  status: 'completing',<br/>  message: 'Finalizando upload...<br/>  Pode levar alguns minutos.'<br/>}
    
    Note over DLQ: Worker processa job (assíncrono)
    
    DLQ->>+S3: CompleteMultipartUpload<br/>(retry com backoff)
    S3-->>-DLQ: 200 OK
    
    DLQ->>+DB: UPDATE media_files<br/>SET status='processing'
    DB-->>-DLQ: OK
    
    DLQ->>API: Invoke Lambda ProcessVS
    
    Note over FE: Frontend faz polling<br/>GET /media/{id}/status
    
    FE->>+API: GET /media/{id}/status
    API->>+DB: SELECT status FROM media_files
    DB-->>-API: {status: 'processing'}
    API-->>-FE: {status: 'processing'}
    
    FE-->>FE: Mostrar spinner<br/>"Processando áudio..."
```

